findings.suggested_fix:
Call all hooks unconditionally before any early return:

export function Profile({ user }: { user: { name: string } | null }) {
  const [editing, setEditing] = useState(false);
  if (!user) return null;
  // ...
}

Also remove the eslint-disable comment so the rules-of-hooks rule can check the component again.

Read the latest value through a ref:

const draftRef = useRef(draft);
draftRef.current = draft;
useEffect(() => {
  const id = setInterval(() => save(draftRef.current), 5000);
  return () => clearInterval(id);
}, [save]);

Or include draft in the dependency list. Remove the eslint-disable comment once the dependencies are correct.

Return a cleanup from the effect:

useEffect(() => {
  const onResize = () => setWidth(window.innerWidth);
  window.addEventListener("resize", onResize);
  return () => window.removeEventListener("resize", onResize);
}, []);
